<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to June 14.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to June 14.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly</p>
<p>harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June)</p>
<p>sugar crop to June 14 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week June 8-June 14</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97	 458,751 tns	 45,535 tns     9.93 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	 114,982 tns	 10,125 tns     8.81 pct</p>
<p>     94-95	 296,305 tns	 33,790 tns    11.40 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to June 14</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    41,691,363 tns    4,495,663 tns    10.78 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    39,973,565 tns    4,359,232 tns    10.91 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    39,869,713 tns    4,252,911 tns    10.67 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 21 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 10 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 20 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
</text>
